<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zalim Singh Jhala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1739–1824</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zalim Singh Jhala was the regent and real ruler of Kota in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a> from the 1770s until his death in 1824. A capable administrator and soldier, he reformed the revenue, kept Kota safe from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> and Pindari raids and allied with the British in 1817. In 1838 the British separated part of Kota to form Jhalawar for his descendants.</p></div>
